WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:01.329
Wolverine.

00:00:01.329 --> 00:00:02.329
Logan.

00:00:02.329 --> 00:00:03.329
James Howlett.

00:00:03.329 --> 00:00:07.009
Whatever you call him, the facts remain the
same: Wolverine is the best there is at what

00:00:07.009 --> 00:00:09.860
he does — and what he does usually isn't
very nice.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.639
But just how big a jerk is he in the comics?

00:00:12.639 --> 00:00:16.080
Here's a look at the most terrible things
Wolverine has ever done.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.570
He drowned his own son

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:22.140
Wolverine has a whole lot of descendents,
which is just par for the course for a near-immortal

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.050
animal-guy with poor impulse control.

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:28.210
The worst of them all, though, is his son
Daken, who inherited his father's mutant abilities

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:31.770
and bloodlust, only without that pesky conscience
to go along for the ride.

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:36.270
A trained assassin, Daken actually defeated
his dad and stuck him in a vat of water to

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:41.020
drown, since — even with a healing factor
— Wolverine still needs to wolver-breathe.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:45.600
However, after a timely rescue by Deadpool,
Wolverine got free, tracked down Daken, and

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:48.970
in a bit of karmic retribution, drowned him
in a puddle.

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:50.010
Bad dad!

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:51.550
More kids, more murder

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:55.480
The Mongrels were a team of supervillains
sent to fight Wolverine by a secret group

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:59.630
of bad guys who called themselves the Red
Right Hand, since apparently every good team

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:01.190
name was already taken.

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:05.050
After being trapped in hell — don't ask
— Wolverine gets free and goes on one of

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:07.870
his patented revenge benders,

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:11.320
"Revenge Rampage!"

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:13.310
killing all the Mongrels in the process.

00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:16.741
It's only after they're all dead that the
Red Right Hand reveals the Mongrels were all

00:01:16.741 --> 00:01:21.510
children of Wolverine, and it was all a big
ploy to make him feel really bad about himself.

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:22.780
Way to think small, guys!

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:25.060
He tortured an American soldier

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:29.310
Frank Simpson was an abused, mentally disturbed
child who killed his own mother.

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:33.100
Things somehow actually got worse for Frank,
though, when Wolverine murdered his father

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:37.310
and then forced him to join a government program
that manufactures superhumans.

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:41.270
After emerging from the program a total wreck,
Frank was sent to Vietnam, where a sadistic

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:45.310
Wolverine then tortured and brainwashed him
into becoming the mindless murder machine

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:46.750
known as Nuke.

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:47.750
So….

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:49.900
Why exactly is Logan considered a good guy
again?

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:52.660
Oh, right, because Hugh Jackman sings.

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:54.200
"Who am I?

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:59.880
I'm Wolverine!"

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.500
He set up Colossus for a beatdown

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:06.880
Wolverine's fellow X-Men Colossus and Kitty
Pryde have long had an on-again, off-again

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:07.880
romance.

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:11.720
Back when Colossus first dumped Kitty, though,
Wolverine was none too happy about how his

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:13.450
comrade handled the situation.

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:17.350
So he decided to teach Colossus a lesson by
getting him drunk and then letting Juggernaut

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:20.090
deliver a massive beatdown on the overmatched
hero.

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:21.090
Yup.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:24.810
While Nightcrawler wants to intervene and
help their friend, Wolverine refuses, insisting

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:28.000
that Colossus has it coming for being such
a heartless cad.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:32.211
He's not necessarily wrong, and compared to
repeatedly murdering his own children, it's

00:02:32.211 --> 00:02:34.780
pretty low on the list of bad things Wolverine
has done.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:35.920
But, you know.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.459
Think twice before enlisting Logan as your
wingman.

00:02:38.459 --> 00:02:40.060
An infinite number of jerks

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:43.599
In the comics, there's an infinite number
of alternate universes, meaning there's an

00:02:43.599 --> 00:02:46.819
infinite number of jerks named Wolverine running
around doing horrible things.

00:02:46.819 --> 00:02:47.860
Don't believe it?

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:52.460
Well, say hello to Wolverine the vampire lord,
who, after being turned into a vampire by

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:54.850
Dracula, infects the rest of the X-Men.

00:02:54.850 --> 00:02:57.820
And then they go on a murderous spree, killing
the rest of the superheroes.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:58.820
Like you do.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:02.360
Then there's the Age of Apocalypse Logan,
who called himself Weapon Omega.

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:06.660
His plan was to help alien beings called the
Celestials completely wipe out all humanity,

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:08.080
because… reasons.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:11.630
Naturally, in the course of the story, he
also murdered his own daughter, because that

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:13.950
is apparently just how Wolverine rolls.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:17.870
Then there's the infamous, original Old Man
Logan storyline, which was one of the inspirations

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:19.040
for the movie Logan.

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:22.970
In the comic book version, Logan swears off
violence after he is tricked by an illusionist

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:25.410
named Mysterio into murdering all of the X-Men.

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:28.300
This is what happens when you never learn
anger control, dude.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.489
Ultimate creep

00:03:29.489 --> 00:03:34.379
As bad as all those other versions of Wolverine
are, the worst has to be the Ultimate Universe

00:03:34.379 --> 00:03:37.930
Wolverine, who is consistently written as
an amoral villain who just happens to be working

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:38.930
for the X-Men.

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:42.550
It's impossible to list all of his misdeeds,
but among the worst are the time he straight

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:46.840
up murdered a scared mutant kid because he
was worried about bad publicity for mutants

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:49.150
after the boy lost control of his powers.

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:52.830
Then there's the time he tried to kill Cyclops
because he wanted to make out with Jean Grey.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:57.200
But probably the worst is when Jean Grey mind-swapped
Logan with the teenage Peter Parker to teach

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:01.680
Logan a lesson, only to have Wolverine use
it as an excuse for some very inappropriate

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:04.269
interactions with underage high school girls.

00:04:04.269 --> 00:04:06.680
Face it: Wolverine is just messed up.

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:08.120
Thanks for watching!

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.610
